1916:        on_D: { action: "Cancel workflow", status: "CANCELLED", release_lock: step_release_lock }
1918:      step_update_tracking:
1924:      step_loop_decision:
1925:        action: "Return to step_read_state for next iteration"
1926:        goto: step_read_state
1931:  phase_synthesis:
1935:      step_fanout_merge:
1946:      step_hydrate_summary_metrics:
1971:          - reason: "When this session's loop left phase_loop for synthesis, keep the reason it bound on that exit: the STOP reason from step_check_convergence (maxIterationsReached, converged, blockedStop or error), maxDurationReached from step_check_max_duration, or manualStop from an on_C exit. Never re-derive it from rows: no state row carries any of those reasons before closeout, and a resumed run's log still holds the earlier session's userPaused and stuckRecovery rows. Otherwise use the latest synthesis/recovery stop reason in {state_paths.state_log} after the latest 'resumed' or 'run_extended' row, if present. On a fan-out root (direct lineage state logs exist and the root state log holds no such stop row): take each lineage that {state_paths.packet_dir}/orchestration-summary.json lists with status succeeded, and read the stopReason of the last row carrying a stopReason in {state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/<label>/deep-research-state.jsonl; when they agree use it, when they differ use the one whose row has the latest timestamp, since the run ended when that lineage stopped. Only when neither yields a reason, the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused, maxDurationReached.)"
1994:        on_A: { proceed_to: step_read_all_iterations }
1998:      step_read_all_iterations:
2007:      step_emit_resource_map:
2026:      step_compile_research:
2050:      step_convergence_report:
2113:        on_A: { proceed_to: step_writeback_spec_findings }
2118:          proceed_to: step_update_config_status
2120:      step_writeback_spec_findings:
2133:              release_lock: step_release_lock
2142:      step_validate_post_synthesis_spec_doc:
2147:      step_update_config_status:
2153:      step_refresh_completed_dashboard:
2162:      step_telemetry_heartbeat_terminal:
2172:      step_stage_artifact_dir:
2177:        note: "Skill-owned contract: without this stage step, operators who do `git add research-report.md` lose the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, etc.). Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the audit trail intact. Operators retain commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` to unstage anything before commit. Failure is non-fatal: log warning and continue. The repository .gitignore already keeps the live lock file, the pause and run-now sentinels, and the legacy projection watermark directory out of the index, so the command names no exclude pathspec: git add exits 1 when an exclude names a path that is ignored and present, as the lock is while the run still holds it (step_release_lock runs later, in phase_save). locks-and-fencing-v1, ledgers, deltas, iterations and the state log stay staged."
2210:      step_compose_save_payload:
2232:      step_generate_context:
2238:      step_verify_save:
2243:      step_release_lock:
2278:  consecutive_failures: "See step_check_convergence rule 1a. The script counts trailing failed iterations from the state log and returns stop reason error."
2300:    - modify_config_after_initialization_outside_its_writer_steps  # step_extend_completed_run, step_frontier_budget and step_update_config_status
2319:      - "Live breadth growth is the opt-in --depth-mode=expansive frontier (step_frontier_seed, step_frontier_admit); waves stay reference-only."

